            "code": "import Mathlib\n\nstructure RingBuffer (T : Type) where\n  capacity : Nat\n  view : List T\n\ndef RingBuffer.is_valid {T} (rb : RingBuffer T) : Prop :=\n  rb.capacity > 0 \u2227 rb.view.length \u2264 rb.capacity\n\n-- Precondition definitions\n@[reducible, simp]\ndef dequeue_precond {T} (rb : RingBuffer T) : Prop :=\n  -- !benchmark @start precond\n  rb.is_valid \u2227 rb.view.length > 0\n  -- !benchmark @end precond\n\n-- !benchmark @start auxcode\n-- !benchmark @end auxcode\n\n-- Main function definition\n-- Returns (value, new_ringbuffer)\ndef dequeue {T} (rb : RingBuffer T)\n    (h_precond : dequeue_precond rb) : T \u00d7 RingBuffer T :=\n  -- !benchmark @start code\n  (rb.view.head (List.ne_nil_of_length_pos h_precond.2),\n   { capacity := rb.capacity, view := rb.view.tail })\n  -- !benchmark @end code\n\n-- Postcondition definitions\n@[reducible, simp]\ndef dequeue_postcond {T} (rb : RingBuffer T) (result : T \u00d7 RingBuffer T)\n    (_ : dequeue_precond rb) : Prop :=\n  -- !benchmark @start postcond\n  let (val, new_rb) := result\n  new_rb.is_valid \u2227\n  new_rb.capacity = rb.capacity \u2227\n  -- Concise & Proof-Free: Old view is (val :: new_view)\n  rb.view = val :: new_rb.view\n  -- !benchmark @end postcond\n\n-- !benchmark @start lemma\n-- !benchmark @end lemma\n\n-- Proof content\ntheorem dequeue_postcond_satisfied {T} (rb : RingBuffer T)\n    (h_precond : dequeue_precond rb) :\n    dequeue_postcond rb (dequeue rb h_precond) h_precond := by\n  -- !benchmark @start proof\n  obtain \u27e8\u27e8hcap, hlen\u27e9, hpos\u27e9 := h_precond\n  have hne : rb.view \u2260 [] := List.ne_nil_of_length_pos hpos\n  refine \u27e8\u27e8hcap, ?_\u27e9, rfl, ?_\u27e9\n  \u00b7 exact le_trans (by simp [List.length_tail]) hlen\n  \u00b7 exact (List.cons_head_tail hne).symm\n  -- !benchmark @end proof\n",
            "comment": "`Solution.lean` compiles cleanly with no warnings, no `sorry`.\n\n**Approach**\n\n- **Implementation** (`code` region): the front element is `rb.view.head`, whose non-emptiness proof comes straight from the precondition `rb.view.length > 0` via `List.ne_nil_of_length_pos`. The new buffer keeps `capacity` and takes `rb.view.tail` as its view \u2014 no dependent pattern match needed, which keeps the definition transparent to the proof.\n\n- **Proof** (`proof` region): destructure the precondition into `capacity > 0`, `length \u2264 capacity`, and `length > 0`, then discharge the three conjuncts:\n  - validity: capacity is unchanged, and `(tail).length \u2264 view.length \u2264 capacity`;\n  - capacity preservation: `rfl`, since the field is copied verbatim;\n  - view structure: `List.cons_head_tail`, i.e. `head :: tail = view`, reversed.\n\nThe `auxcode` and `lemma` regions stayed empty; everything outside the four marker regions is untouched."
